      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Frontier Mountains [EoK]\n**Who:**\n- Agent Honeydrop [ _Combine Operative_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 00:01:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Frontier Lumber [item=127744]\n- Frontier Ore [item=127743]\n- Frontier Silk [item=127745]\n- Giant Burlap Sheet [item=127611]\n- Huge Bear Tendon [item=127612]\n- Huge Brute Brain [item=127614]\n- Huge Food Bundle [item=127740]\n- Huge Goblin Leg [item=127613]\n- Huge Resource Bundle [item=127746]\n- Huge Sarnak Tail [item=127601]\n- Huge Wolf Flank [item=127646]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Gasi [ _Blacksmith_]\n- Stak [ _Warmonger_]\n- a Drogan hulk [npc=51293]\n- a Konikor evacuee [npc=51864]\n- a Legion miner [npc=51124]\n- a grove guardian [npc=51280]\n- a highweb spitter [npc=51283]\n- a huge frontier bear [npc=51125]\n- a huge frontier brute [npc=51300]\n- an experimental behemoth [npc=51261]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Concerned Citizens [quest=8272]\n- Contacting the Leadership [quest=8385]\n- Disappearing Dragons [quest=8262]\n- Pentalateral Negotiations [quest=8453]\n- Sneaky Sarnak [quest=8392]\n**Era:** | !Empires of Kunark\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Nov 14 07:21:19 2016\nModified: Sun Sep 8 03:20:59 2024 | | Prerequisite: Concerned Citizens [quest=8272], Contacting the Leadership [quest=8385], Disappearing Dragons [quest=8262], Sneaky Sarnak [quest=8392], and Pentalateral Negotiations [quest=8453].\nThis is a shared task.\nSpeak to Agent Honeydrop in Frontier Mountains.\nSay \"help\" to her to get this task.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Speak with Stak the Warmonger. Inside the large central fortress. 0/1 Frontier Mountains\nHe assigns you step two and gives you a giant to escort\n2\\. Lead a Konikor Warmonger to the Western Sarnak Outposts 0/1 Frontier Mountains\nThis step updates at /way 364, 2541, 126 at the west part of the zone not far from the outpost.\n3\\. Kill sarnak for the Konikor Warmonger 0/5 Frontier Mountains\nYour accomplice heads back and leaves you with five collect tasks. You can find sarnaks in the western part of the zone in the fort neat the waypoint from the previous step.\nA Giant Burlap Sheet will be placed in your inventory.\n4\\. Collect Huge Bear Tendons 0/3 Frontier Mountains\nDrops from a huge frontier bear, not from a frontier bear. You can find bears in the southwestern part of the zone not far from Earthcaller Quill which is on the find tool CTRL F.\n5\\. Collect Huge Goblin Legs 0/3 Frontier Mountains\nHill above Droga entrance. South of the druid rings. Also south wall, east side. Drops from a Drogan hulk.\n6\\. Collect Huge Wolf Flanks 0/3 Frontier Mountains\nNorth center to North east. Drops from a huge frontier wolf, but not from a frontier wolf.\nNote: if none are up kill frontier wolf and wait for respawns.\n7\\. Collect Huge Brute Brains 0/3 Frontier Mountains\nAlong the east wall. Drops from a huge frontier brute, but not from an invading brute or a frontier brute.\n8\\. Collect Huge Sarnak Tails 0/3 Frontier Mountains\nHuge Sarnak Tails can not be prelooted.\nFrom the same fort that was in the prior step. Drops from an experimental behemoth, but not from an enchanted Sydon stalker, a Sarmak peacekeeper or a syldon greenhorn. [Inside fort]\n9\\. Use Giant Burlap Sheet to bundle up all the body parts 0/1 Frontier Mountains\nThis appeared in your inventory at the end of step 3. Just click it. It's not a container and it's tradeable. Clicking puts a Huge Food Bundle in your inventory\n10\\. Travel to Konikor's central fort 0/1 Frontier Mountains\nThis step updates around /way 154, -953, -148 outside the central giant fort on the north wall.\n11\\. Give Huge Food Bundle to a Konikor Evacuee 0/1 Frontier Mountains\nAfter the update on step 10 a Konikor evacuee spawns and follows you. Give Huge Food Bundle to it.\n12\\. Lead a Konikor evacuee to Stak 0/1 Frontier Mountains\nStak is in the giant fort near the north side. Hail Stak for the update. Listen to Stak's Speech.\n13\\. Listen to Stak's speech 0/1 Frontier Mountains\nFollow Stak until he stops. He speaks a bunch of dialogue.\n14\\. Speak with Gasi the Blacksmith 0/1 Frontier Mountains\nGasi the Blacksmith is in the giant fort in the building on the north side. Hail him and you get three more collect steps.\n15\\. Collect Frontier Ore from Legion miners 0/6 Frontier Mountains\nYou can find legion miners near a cave in the southwestern part of the zone near /way -2016, 2306, -324. They respawn fairly quickly, within a few minutes.\n16\\. Collect Frontier Lumber from Grove Guardians 0/6 Frontier Mountains\nYou can find grove guardians near the druid ring in the northwest corner of the zone.\n17\\. Collect Frontier Silk from Highland Weavers 0/6 Frontier Mountains\nThese drop from spiders in the southeastern part of the zone.\n18\\. Use the Giant Burlap Sheet to bundle up all the materials 0/1 Frontier Mountains\nRight click the Giant Burlap Sheet once you have the above materials. This makes a Huge Resource Bundle that shows up in your inventory.\n19\\. Give the Huge Weapon Bundle to Gasi 0/1 Frontier Mountains\nIt's actually called Huge Resource Bundle.\nGasi eagerly grabs the supplies from you. He smiles and shouts, \" XXX bring us stuff for weapons! Soon we ready to war!\n20\\. Speak with Stak 0/1 Frontier Mountains\nYou say, 'Hail, Stak'\nStak nods and says, 'Thanks Barbarian, Time next step. You stay. We take from here.'\nYou gain experience!\nStak says, 'Walk with me if want. I meet with Honey now.'\nStak walks West, and meets Honey\nStak say, 'Goo see you, Honey. Ready go?'\nAgent Honeydrop smiles at you and nods in greeting.\nAgent Honeydrop says, 'I trust my agent coordinated all of the preparations with you, Stak? Is everything taken care of?'\nStak nods and says, 'Agent good. Konikor angry, ready fight. Have weapons. Below close.'\nAgent Honeydrop says, 'Good. Then let's get going. We need to convince your reluctant friends below to join our cause quickly if we don't want to be overrun. I trust you have a few more tricks up your sleeve, Stak.'\nStaks says, 'Of course, Honey.'\nAgent Honeydrop says, 'You're testing my patience, Stak. I've told you a hundred times to call me Agent, not Honey. I know you do it on purpose!'\nAgent Honeydrop sighs.\nAgent Honeydrop says, 'You did well here, Agent. I'll be in touch soon. Our next brunch will be glorious.'\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n638pp\nExperience or 10 AA's\n**Submitted by:** Deloehne\n- 638pp, Experience or 10 AA's",
